From 0105819b21738dbe96beea7c87a3e9a316abda20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:59:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban active_pr: awaited-review head re-read before
 release, one gh read, one parked-run definition, strict wait-check parse

Follow-up to the 4 non-blocking nits of PR #1995 (review 5888333701, card t_01a1d417c6c8fd9c).

1. pr_head TTL: a cached head may only REFUSE an awaited-review release. A match is
   confirmed by a head read at most RELEASE_HEAD_MAX_AGE_SECONDS (5 s) old, so a
   force-push after the approval can no longer match the approved sha from a read up to
   OPEN_TTL_SECONDS (300 s) old. A failed re-read is unknown (hold). Mismatches still
   come from the cache (no gh call per held tick).
2. One gh read: _gh_pr_state now asks for state,comments,headRefOid and records the OPEN
   head in kanban_db_dispatch_pr_state._heads; pr_head reads that entry and refreshes it
   through the same read (which also refreshes pr_state's cache). The separate
   `gh pr view --json state,headRefOid` in kanban_awaited_review is gone.
3. kanban_pr_same_run_park.latest_parked_run is the single "parked run" definition
   (latest executed run, the assignee's, outcome scheduled/continued, ended_at set);
   reported_then_parked and kanban_awaited_review._park both use it, and the tie park
   event must be the kind the run's outcome names. A run that wrote its park event and
   then crashed/was reclaimed/timed out (or never ended) no longer releases the tie.
4. _WAIT_CHECK now matches only the whole card-wait idiom with wait-check's own flags
   (--gateway/--board/--until/--from). `... t_x && false`, `| grep`, and a second line
   previously named t_x; now they name nothing (fail closed). Wrapped probes (bash -lc,
   timeout, paths, env) and gateway/request awaiting refs are pinned as naming nothing;
   a real park's recorded `awaiting` kind card (inferred from a live card named in the
   probe) still names it, which a test pins.

Proof:
- RED on origin/main base (src reverted, tests kept): 17 of 38 new tests fail, covering
  every point (force-push, shared read x2, outcome/ended_at ties x10 + helper, && / | / \n
  probes x3). GREEN: 41/41 in test_kanban_active_pr_awaited_head.py.
- Mutation: 13/13 mutants killed (cached release, no cached refusal, stale head kept on
  refresh, max_age ignored, non-OPEN head recorded, failure not cached, pr_head without
  store, outcome/ended_at/assignee/kind dropped from the parked run, regex tail opened,
  flags dropped).
- Replay over the hub's real rows (hub-read, read-only; kanban + kanban-hermes): 1 of 1982
  park probes changes (t_01a183029f279d66 `wait-check task A && wait-check task B`; its
  recorded awaiting still names A, so no release changes); 0 of 98 latest runs carrying a
  park event change their parked-run verdict.
- 264 kanban test files importing the changed modules: 4778 passed, 0 failed.
